WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.335
At a high level,

00:00:01.335 --> 00:00:05.065
the brain and nervous system are made of cells and networks that communicate through

00:00:05.065 --> 00:00:06.300
patterns of activity.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.720
Neurons connect with other neurons,

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.650
and those connections participate in pathways that support perception, movement, thought,

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.040
memory, emotion, and action.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.260
For this course, the practical point is that learning is not just receiving information.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.460
It involves changes in how patterns are activated and used.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.690
Patterns can be strengthened or weakened through repeated use.

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:26.986
A skill that is practiced often, with attention and feedback, can become easier to access.

00:00:26.986 --> 00:00:31.140
A behavior that is repeatedly triggered by the same cue can become more automatic.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.720
A strategy that is rarely used may remain effortful.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.105
This is often described as use-dependent change:

00:00:36.105 --> 00:00:39.940
the nervous system adapts partly in response to what is repeatedly used.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:44.715
Attention, emotion, repetition, feedback, and context all influence learning.

00:00:44.715 --> 00:00:46.680
Attention helps select what is processed.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:50.080
Repetition gives the system multiple chances to stabilize a pattern.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.750
Feedback helps correct the pattern.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:55.054
Context provides cues that tell the learner when and how to use the skill.

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:58.815
Emotion and relevance can influence whether an experience receives enough priority to be

00:00:58.815 --> 00:01:00.010
remembered and revisited.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:03.860
The practical implication is clear: people adapt to the systems around them.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:07.580
Training, routines, incentives, tools, and environments all shape what gets repeated.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.100
If a workplace rewards rushed work, rushed patterns may become normal.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.310
If a learning design rewards retrieval, correction, and reflection,

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.700
those patterns become easier to use.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.860
Behavior design is not separate from learning; it is part of the learning environment.
